From b9290d17cbb81c40e02eaaec1165f47756ad11fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usman Akram <102724070+UsmaNaman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] util/fast-hash: compute standard XXH3 on little-endian
 hosts

xemu's configure sets auto_features=disabled, which meson also applies to
the xxhash subproject's cpu-little-endian feature, so the build passes
-DXXH_CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN=0 on little-endian hosts (seen on arm64 macOS).
XXH3_64bits then disagrees with every other XXH3 implementation, so
texture dump hashes could not be reproduced outside xemu. Undefine it and
inline xxhash in this file so the endianness is auto-detected.

Changes every fast_hash value; they are only used as in-process cache keys
except the GL renderer's on-disk shader cache list, which will miss once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZfY8PfkRfJCjArnYegSSy
---
 util/fast-hash.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/util/fast-hash.c b/util/fast-hash.c
index 84e9c3c..cf03b1d 100644
--- a/util/fast-hash.c
+++ b/util/fast-hash.c
@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 #include "qemu/fast-hash.h"
+/*
+ * configure's auto_features=disabled also disables the xxhash subproject's
+ * cpu-little-endian feature, which passes XXH_CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN=0 on little
+ * endian hosts and yields non-standard XXH3 values. Let xxhash detect it.
+ */
+#undef XXH_CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN
+#define XXH_INLINE_ALL
 #include <xxhash.h>
 
 uint64_t fast_hash(const uint8_t *data, size_t len)
-- 
